From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:31:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't restore caching type after a failed sysmem
 allocation

When nv_alloc_system_pages() fails partway through, it calls
nv_free_system_pages() for cleanup. For non-cached allocations, that
function unconditionally restores the caching type with
nv_set_memory_type(at, NV_MEMORY_WRITEBACK). It does this even though
the type was never changed to UC, which only happens after all pages
have been allocated.

nv_set_memory_type() walks all at->num_pages entries of the page table.
On a partial allocation, the unpopulated entries have phys_addr 0, so
set_pages_array_wb() gets the struct page of PFN 0 for each of them.
memtype_free() then finds no matching entry and logs one line per page:

  x86/PAT: <comm>:<pid> freeing invalid memtype [mem 0x00000000-0x00000fff]

A single failed allocation under memory pressure can produce tens of
thousands of these lines. That overruns the kernel log buffer
("/dev/kmsg buffer overrun") and drops the messages that would explain
the actual failure.

Track whether the caching type was changed with a new memtype_set flag,
and restore it only in that case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7692cd97bedde1db1492306a665ea4efc3ef3e20)
---
 kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h |  1 +
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c        | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
index 8e432dee..e4471f38 100644
--- a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
+++ b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
@@ -929,6 +929,7 @@ typedef struct nv_alloc_s {
         NvBool coherent    : 1;
         NvBool carveout    : 1;
         NvBool pool        : 1;
+        NvBool memtype_set : 1;
     } flags;
     unsigned int   cache_type;
     unsigned int   num_pages;
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
index 2b32e4b3..c4ec2bdc 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-vm.c
@@ -1027,9 +1027,16 @@ nv_free_system_pages
 
     nv_account_mm_free(at->accounting_mm_work);
 
-    if (at->cache_type != NV_MEMORY_CACHED)
+    //
+    // Only restore the caching type if nv_alloc_system_pages() changed it.
+    // On a failed allocation, the page table is only partially populated and
+    // the remaining entries would make set_pages_array_wb() operate on PFN 0,
+    // flooding the kernel log with "x86/PAT: freeing invalid memtype" messages.
+    //
+    if (at->flags.memtype_set)
     {
         nv_set_memory_type(at, NV_MEMORY_WRITEBACK);
+        at->flags.memtype_set = NV_FALSE;
     }
 
     for (i = 0; i < num_pages; i++)
@@ -1144,6 +1151,7 @@ nv_alloc_system_pages
     if (at->cache_type != NV_MEMORY_CACHED)
     {
         nv_set_memory_type(at, NV_MEMORY_UNCACHED);
+        at->flags.memtype_set = NV_TRUE;
     }
 
     return NV_OK;
